I'm definitely learning with this game now.
This ascension had only three deaths between it and my last ascension
last week, by far a personal best for me.
One was insta-death, one foolishness, and one was indirectly due to a
typo.

v3 had some luck on her side from the start.  Next to the dlvl 2
stairs, there was a small armor shop containing a cloak of
displacement, oilskin cloak, and dwarvish mithril.  I stole the cloaks
and bought the armor ASAP.  MC3, good AC and displacement along with a
dipped Excalibur.

Continued to have good luck - many large general stores were generated
in the upper dungeon.  In addition, minetown was swarming with lamps.
Only one magical, which I ascended with unused.  Between all the shops
I racked up 3 magic markers.  No hostile dwarves dropped a pickaxe, so
I just left it for now.  Altar was cross-aligned and I did not see
another altar until very deep into the dungeon, so no holy water to be
found.  Sokoban yielded BoH, and also a horn from a trapped unicorn.

Also picked up my first smokey potion which was generated blessed.  I
locked myself in a room, wrote the E-word, and took a chance.... which
generated a wish.  +2 GDSM pretty early on!

Got the luckstone from minetown, resistances were fairly easy to get
this game as well.  Between fantastic monster drops and multiple
shops, I was able to get speed boots and gauntlets of power.  Still no
reflection though.
Around level 22 I ran across a bones file from v2, who passed out from
eating a rotten troll and was pummeled to death.  I hauled the loot
upstairs and uncursed it.  That being said, the BoH was still blessed,
and the contents seemed to be untouched.  6 potions of holy water as
well!  Not too much great armor, etc, but I filled out my potions,
scrolls, wands, and rings pretty well.  Got a free action ring, which
I put on.

I breezed through Medusa, used telepathy to see what was in the
castle.  I took some time to think and realized I needed to be better
prepared.  I took the alignment hit and killed a dwarf that was
digging in the mines(one of the few times I went upwards instead of
pressing on).  Picked up some candles as well.  Headed back and used
the dwarf's pickaxe to shatter Perseus and take a shield of
reflection.

Assaulted the castle from the rear and ate orange and black dragons
for my last resistances.  For the first time in a while, no good
equipment in the castle(except helmet of opposite alignment), but at
that point, I was pretty well off.  The only time I came close to
dying was foolishly trying to rush some liches in the castle with low
HP.  I got surrounded and had my first prayer inside an air elemental
with 10 HP.  I finished off the castle and took the wand.  I was never
below 90% of my max HP after that incident.

Before moving on, I desparately needed some AC help.  I was only at
about -15 AC or so.  I was able to locate Ludios without to much
trouble.  Before entering, I had a passing fancy for Grayswandir, so I
wished for it.  I still have no clue why... First monster out of the
door was a cockatrice which left a corpse. :)  I had never wielded one
to smite mass enemies, so I gave it a whirl.  About 50+ statues later,
and most of the castle was clear.  My next setback was in a chest in
the barracks.  I didn't check enough times for traps and got jolted.
Ring of free action AND my wishing wand were destroyed.  I was much
more worried about lack of free action.  Sure enough, one of the
mosters in the castle briefly paralyzed me.  I survived and used the
gold to buy AC from another cross-aligned temple.

I checked all my stashes and then remembered that I had 2 bags of
holding. Sure enough, one of them contained another free action ring.
I definitely set myself up for a YASD walking around without one.  I
did the quest, no problems there.  Further down, a rabid rat ran
across yet another cross-aligned altar.  I keep forgetting that just
about any monster can be sacrificed to convert an altar... *facepalm*
One rabid rat corpse later, and I have a co-aligned alter.  Shortly
following that, I got Mojo.

I did some alchemy twice in the game, as healing, etc was VERY
plentiful.  Ended up with over 300HP.

I descended into hell, using Excalibur to prevent level drain, and
also for searching traps.  I used Mojo for ranged attacks.  I foo-
proofed what I could, but my AC was still terrible.  I had not
discovered charging or genocide, and enchant armor was scarce.
Finally, well into hell, I found genocide and wiped out L.  I later
wrote another one with a marker and got mimics right before Orcus town
as well, another first.  Payed off too.  Another marker was procured
from Orcus town as well as a scroll of charging.  A few steps away
from the stairs on the level above I also found a cloak of
protection.  I wrote enchant armor until I was blue in the face, using
remaining charges to write utility scrolls like gold detection, magic
mapping, and identify.  Got my AC to about -45 or more.  I also
realized that before putting on the cloak of protection I had been
waltzing around with only MC2, which explained a lot of my problems,
like being slimed and other calamities.

Took the life saving amulet from Vlad's tower and picked up some more
rings.  For some reason, I started finding tons of free action rings.
In all, over half a dozen.  I stopped picking them up after 3 spares.

Pushed on to the end game and marked the square.  Before cracking open
the wizard's tower, I typo'd TWICE and fell in the moat.  I lost some
potions, but not too bad. I killed Rodney using Mojo, dang wands just
weren't cutting it.  I got caught up in the sanctum and really had
difficulty getting through the mess of insects and demons summoning
other baddies.  Mysterious force was annoying, but bearable.
Periodically, I would hammer the wizard to death.  Malignant auras
were a problem, but I had some remove curse scrolls.

Plane of earth - zapped rodney with the wand this time, never saw him
again.  Used gold detection and moved on.  I then realized that the
orb of fate could help find portals as well, which was good since I
didn't have any more methods of confusion(or gold scrolls).  Planes
were an absolute breeze for once.  I used another passing fancy wish
for scrolls of genocide and genocided ';' on the plane of water.
Totally unnecessary, but it REALLY cleared the place out.

I took the middle on the planes(pestilence).  I squeezed through,
avoiding fights and found that the altar was chaotic.  Again, in
another first for me, I donned the helm of opposite alignment from the
castle and offered the amulet.

